For tidiness, the input component and its authoring MonoBehaviour live in one file:

    // PlayerMoveInput.cs
    public struct PlayerMoveInput : IInputComponentData { public float2 Move; }
    public class PlayerMoveInputAuthoring : MonoBehaviour { }

You drag the authoring component onto the capsule prefab in the inspector. It appears. You save. It bakes. The capsule spawns, replicates, is owned, is routed, and has no input component at all — and nothing in the console mentions it. Reopening the prefab shows the component slot present but blank.
